@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}
<h1>@ViewData["Title"]</h1>

<div class="mt-2">
    Privacy Policy
</div>
<div class="mt-2">
    1. Introduction
</div>
<div class="mt-2">
    Revalion Software operates the RevalW web application and the RevalM mobile application (collectively, the “Services”).
    This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, store, and protect personal data when you use our Services.
</div>
<div>
    By using RevalW or RevalM, you agree to the collection and use of information in accordance with this Privacy Policy.
</div>
<div class="mt-2">
    2. Scope of the Services
</div>
<div class="mt-2">
    Revalion Software provides a platform for:
</div>
<div>
    Organization and user management
</div>
<div>
    Creating and managing form configurations and evaluation logic
</div>
<div>
    Performing field evaluations via a mobile application
</div>
<div>
    Synchronizing evaluation results between mobile and web platforms
</div>
<div>
    Generating PDF reports and documentation
</div>
<div>
    The Services are currently under active development, and features may change over time.
</div>
<div class="mt-2">
    3. Information We Collect
</div>
<div class="mt-2">
    3.1 Information You Provide
</div>
<div>
    We may collect the following information when you register or use the Services:
</div>
<div>
    Account information: name, email address, username, role (creator, admin, user)
</div>
<div>
    Organization data: organization name, internal user assignments
</div>
<div>
    Evaluation data: form inputs, measured values, evaluation results
</div>
<div>
    Documents and templates: configuration text, generated PDFs
</div>
<div class="mt-2">
    3.2 Automatically Collected Information
</div>
<div class="mt-2">
    When using the Services, we may automatically collect:
</div>
<div>
    Log data (access times, actions performed, error logs)
</div>
<div>
    Synchronization status between RevalM and RevalW
</div>
<div class="mt-2">
    4. Mobile Application (RevalM)
</div>
<div class="mt-2">
    The RevalM mobile application may:
</div>
<div>
    Store evaluation data locally on your device for offline use
</div>
<div>
    Synchronize stored data with RevalW once an internet connection is available
</div>
<div>
    Access device storage solely for saving and transferring evaluation data
</div>
<div>
    RevalM does not access personal contacts, photos, or unrelated device data.
</div>
<div class="mt-2">
    5. How We Use Your Information
</div>
<div class="mt-2">
    We use collected information to:
</div>
<div>
    Provide and operate the Services
</div>
<div>
    Manage organizations, users, and permissions
</div>
<div>
    Perform and process evaluations
</div>
<div>
    Generate reports and PDF documents
</div>
<div>
    Synchronize data between web and mobile applications
</div>
<div>
    Improve functionality, performance, and reliability
</div>
<div>
    Ensure system security and prevent misuse
</div>
<div class="mt-2">
    6. Data Sharing
</div>
<div class="mt-2">
    We do not sell or rent personal data.
</div>
<div>
    Data may be shared only:
</div>
<div>
    Within your organization, according to assigned roles and permissions
</div>
<div>
    With service providers required to operate the infrastructure (e.g., hosting, storage), under confidentiality obligations
</div>
<div class="mt-2">
    7. Data Storage and Security
</div>
<div class="mt-2">
    Data is stored on secure servers using reasonable technical and organizational safeguards
</div>
<div>
    Access is restricted based on user roles (creator, admin, user)
</div>
<div>
    Offline data stored on mobile devices remains under the user’s control until synchronized
</div>
<div>
    Despite our efforts, no system can be guaranteed 100% secure.
</div>
<div class="mt-2">
    8. Data Retention
</div>
<div class="mt-2">
    We retain data only as long as necessary to:
</div>
<div>
    Provide the Services
</div>
<div>
    Organizations control their own evaluation data and may request deletion where applicable.
</div>
<div class="mt-2">
    9. Your Rights
</div>
<div class="mt-2">
    Depending on your jurisdiction, you may have the right to:
</div>
<div>
    Access your personal data
</div>
<div>
    Correct inaccurate data
</div>
<div>
    Request deletion of your data
</div>
<div>
    Restrict or object to certain processing
</div>
<div>
    Requests can be made by contacting us at the email address below.
</div>
<div class="mt-2">
    10. Children’s Privacy
</div>
<div class="mt-2">
    The Services are not intended for children under 18.
</div>
<div>
    We do not knowingly collect personal data from children.
</div>
<div class="mt-2">
    11. Changes to This Privacy Policy
</div>
<div class="mt-2">
    We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time.
</div>
<div>
    Changes will be posted on this page.
</div>
<div class="mt-2">
    12. Contact Information
</div>
<div class="mt-2">
    If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or data handling, please contact:
</div>
<div>
    Revalion Software
</div>
<div>
    📧 Email: <a href="mailto:revalion22@hotmail.com">revalion22@hotmail.com</a>
</div>
<div>
    🌐 Website: <a href="https://revalion.eu">revalion.eu</a>
</div>
<div class="mt-2">
    13. Development Status Disclaimer
</div>
<div class="mt-2">
    This project is currently under active development.
</div>
<div>
    Features, data handling mechanisms, and storage methods may evolve as the platform matures.
</div>
